//? Title: Truncated binary: complete codes across uint64 alphabets
//? Subtitle: Actual native state, retained fixtures and explicit limits
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Encoding equally likely symbols from a non-power-of-two alphabet wastes bits in
a fixed-width code. Truncated binary assigns two neighboring lengths while
keeping the stream prefix-decodable.
)

\toc

> The method

For n≥1, k=floor(log2 n) and u=2^(k+1)−n. Encode v<u in k bits, otherwise encode
v+u in k+1 bits. Decode k bits x; if x≥u, append one more bit then subtract u.
Kraft equality u/2^k+(n−u)/2^(k+1)=1 proves completeness. Mean length is
k+(n−u)/n, between log2 n and log2 n+1. A singleton alphabet uses zero bits; its
symbol count must be supplied externally.

> Simple worked example

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/truncated_binary_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto bits = a::truncated_binary_encode({0, 1, 2, 3, 4}, 5);
    auto values = a::truncated_binary_decode(bits, 5, 5);
    std::print("| alphabet | actual bits | decoded |\n|---:|---|---|\n|5|`{}`|`{}`|\n",
               bits, values);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "n5; k2; three short symbols");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("Actual stream length {}", bits.size()));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0}, std::format("Actual decoded {}", values));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/truncated_binary_tiny.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| alphabet | actual bits | decoded |
|---:|---|---|
|5|`[false, false, false, true, true, false, true, true, false, true, true, true]`|`[0, 1, 2, 3, 4]`|
