> Interpretation and limits

Wide intermediate arithmetic prevents shift-by64. The decoder now requires
exactly the requested count and complete consumption: truncated and trailing
streams throw. n0, out-of-range symbols and negative counts are rejected. This
is a prefix code with two lengths, not a fixed-length code.

Every figure is saved locally by its complete editable program. No separate
reconstruction supplies algorithm state. Counters describe the selected events,
not elapsed time or peak memory.

